course: dictionary
lesson: 6018
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the dictionary lists each one as a separate number. To choose the right one, look at the sentence around the word. In «Saudi Arabia contains Mecca and Medina, the two holiest cities of Islam», Medina is a place, so it means a city.
explain: A medina can also be the old walled part of a city in North Africa, with narrow streets and markets. Clues like «the old medina» and words such as alleys and souks, in a text about Fez or Marrakesh, show you which meaning is needed.
explain: Capital letters are a clue too. Medina with a capital M is a name, either of a city or of a girl. Ask yourself: does the sentence need a place or a person? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A dictionary lists different meanings of one word as numbered senses.
fact: Medina means a city in Saudi Arabia, the second holiest city in Islam.
fact: The Prophet Muhammad moved from Mecca to Medina in 622 AD; this journey is called the Hijra.
fact: A medina is the old walled part of a city in North Africa, with narrow streets and markets.
fact: Medina is also a girls' name.
exercise: «Saudi Arabia contains Mecca and Medina, the two holiest cities of Islam.» In this sentence, what is Medina? | A girl's name | A type of holy book | A narrow street in an old market | *A city
exercise: «The traveller got lost in the narrow alleys of the old medina in Fez.» What is a medina here? | A river that flows all year | A large desert in Saudi Arabia | *The old walled part of a city, with narrow streets
exercise: «Islamic years are counted from 622, when the Prophet Muhammad moved from Mecca to Medina.» What happened in 622? | *The Prophet Muhammad moved from Mecca to Medina | The first market in Fez opened | Medina became a girls' name | The Prophet Muhammad was born in Medina
test: Maya's new friend is called Medina. What does Medina mean here? | A busy market street | The old walled part of a city | A holy city in Saudi Arabia | *A girl's name
test: Which event does the Hijra describe? | A football match in Riyadh | The building of the first medina in Morocco | *The Prophet Muhammad's journey from Mecca to Medina | A rainy day in Scotland
exam: How can you tell which meaning of a word fits a text? | Guess, because all meanings are the same | *Read the words around it and check the meaning makes sense in the sentence | Always choose the first meaning listed in the dictionary | Pick the longest meaning, because it is the most important
